    "b-05-core-principles-core-design-principles-2": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-core-design-principles-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Core design principles, Sudoku metaphor, run boundaries, metrics, process actors, and former-skill mapping."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-d-comp-orchestrator-trea-3": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-d-comp-orchestrator-trea-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "D-Comp Orchestrator treats a decompilation run as a whole-board reasoning\nproblem. The scheduler does not camp on one target just because it is\nunfinished. It asks where current report and graph evidence make the next useful\nmove easiest, then applies deterministic epoch policy."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-sudoku-metaphor-4": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-sudoku-metaphor-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Sudoku Metaphor"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-treat-decomp-like-sudoku-5": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-treat-decomp-like-sudoku-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Treat decomp like Sudoku:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-a-worker-finding-a-fact-6": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-a-worker-finding-a-fact-6",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A worker finding a fact does not always finish the file it is holding."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-that-fact-can-still-remo-7": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-that-fact-can-still-remo-7",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "That fact can still remove bad possibilities from other targets."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-a-struct-field-source-s-8": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-a-struct-field-source-s-8",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A struct field, source shape, duplicate pattern, naming convention, or"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-negative-result-can-make-9": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-negative-result-can-make-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  negative result can make a different target more constrained."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-the-scheduler-s-job-is-t-10": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-the-scheduler-s-job-is-t-10",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The scheduler's job is to choose the next admitted square based on the entire"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-board-not-to-tunnel-on-11": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-board-not-to-tunnel-on-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  board, not to tunnel on the last square touched."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-in-decomp-terms-a-worke-12": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-in-decomp-terms-a-worke-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "In decomp terms, a worker may discover that a guessed source shape cannot be\nright, that a duplicate reference has a reusable shape, or that a data owner\nblocks several functions. Those outputs become constraints for future target\npackets."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-run-boundary-13": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-run-boundary-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Run Boundary"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-the-run-is-the-unit-of-p-14": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-the-run-is-the-unit-of-p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run is the unit of progress. A source file, worker, symbol, or claim is not\na PR boundary. A run can target a checkpoint such as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "+1.0% matched_code_percent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "\nor "
        },
        {
          "insert": "+5.0% matched_code_percent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and keep integrating verified improvements until\nthat target is reached or useful evidence runs out."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-full-decompilation-remai-15": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-full-decompilation-remai-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Full decompilation remains the long-term objective: exact matched code should\nkeep moving toward "
        },
        {
          "insert": "100%",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The run goal is a checkpoint and stop condition, not\na claim that the project is finished. When the checkpoint is reached, the system\nshould pause the run, emit end-of-run output, and let the operator reallocate\nworkers, raise the checkpoint, package a PR, or start the next run."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-north-star-metric-16": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-north-star-metric-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "North-Star Metric"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-matched-code-percent-i-17": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-matched-code-percent-i-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "matched_code_percent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the north-star metric. It tracks exact matched code\nprogress and is the v1 target for run goals."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-the-default-acceptance-t-18": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-the-default-acceptance-t-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The default acceptance target is reviewable text-section/source code fixes,\ncode-match blockers, and reusable source-shape facts. Data, literal, symbol, and\nsplit cleanup is secondary unless it is explicitly scoped, required for a code\nmatch, or blocking code-match validation."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-fuzzy-match-percent-is-19": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-fuzzy-match-percent-is-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "fuzzy_match_percent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is useful telemetry for target selection and local\ndiagnosis, but it is not the success target. It can be high even when exact\nmatched code progress remains low."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-complete-code-percent-20": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-complete-code-percent-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "complete_code_percent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and linked/unit completeness are useful context, but\nthey are secondary to exact matched-code movement."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-former-skill-surfaces-21": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-former-skill-surfaces-21",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Former Skill Surfaces"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-the-orchestrator-is-the-22": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-the-orchestrator-is-the-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The orchestrator is the top-level run system. Former standalone skill surfaces\nmove down a layer:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-former-surface-new-r-23": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-former-surface-new-r-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "| Former surface | New role inside orchestrator |\n| --- | --- |\n| "
        },
        {
          "insert": "decomp-find",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " | Board scan, candidate-prior features, linked-blocker awareness, and progress metrics. |\n| "
        },
        {
          "insert": "melee-decomp",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " | Worker system prompt and co-located context for one file or symbol: gather evidence, edit source, verify, and stop before guessing. |\n| "
        },
        {
          "insert": "melee-decomp-sweep",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " | Last-resort experimental tooling for bounded source-shape experiments, kept out of default prompt context. |\n| Run scheduler | Deterministic Sudoku player: admit and route targets from the whole board, explicit epoch policy, claims, cooldowns, and every durable fact. |"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-runtime-principle-24": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-runtime-principle-24",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runtime Principle"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-the-orchestrator-itself-25": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-the-orchestrator-itself-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The orchestrator itself is not the main reasoning agent. It is a thin stateful\nrunner that stores facts, target claims, events, prompts, and artifacts. It launches\nworker and boundary-review Pi sessions only when durable state says there is\nwork to do."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-05-core-principles-run-loops-and-guardian-w-26": {
      "id": "b-05-core-principles-run-loops-and-guardian-w-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Run loops and guardian wrappers are process state machines, not hidden board\nagents. The run loop advances the decomp loop from durable events. The guardian\nwrapper preserves liveness from process-health events."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
